    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.invert_node_selection - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.invert_node_selection.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.invert_node_selection()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Invert node selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.invert_node_selection()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Invert node selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.invert_node_selection()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Invert node selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nInvert node selection (select unselected, unselect selected).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L25348-L25423){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.invert_node_selection()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Invert node selection](../assets/graphs/invert-node-selection.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Before: nodes B and E are selected in the accent color. After invert_node_selection the selection flips: A, C, D, and F are selected and B and E are plain.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nReplaces the node selection with its complement: every currently selected node becomes\nunselected and every unselected node becomes selected. With no nodes selected, the result\nis that all nodes are selected.\n\nInverting turns any selection rule into its negation without having to write a second\nrule, which is useful for:\n\n- keeping a subset rather than removing it, e.g., select the nodes to keep, invert, then\n  `delete_nodes_ws()`\n- selecting \"everything except\" a neighborhood, community, or set of hubs\n- selecting all nodes (invert an empty selection) as input to a `*_ws` method\n\nAny edge selection is cleared, since the graph holds a selection of nodes or of edges but\nnot both; to invert an edge selection, use `invert_edge_selection()`. The graph is\nmodified in place and returned for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The same graph (modified in place) for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~invert_edge_selection`) \n\n:   Select the edges that aren't selected.\n\n[](`~deselect_nodes`) \n\n:   Remove nodes from the selection.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nOn a path, the two ends have one neighbor each. Selecting them and inverting the\nselection leaves the four in the middle:\n\n::: {#9906425a .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(6)\ngraph.select_nodes_by_degree(max_degree=1).invert_node_selection()\n\ngraph.count_selected_nodes()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n4\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Far from the center\n\n`metro()` is a made-up city's metro network, each station placed at its `pos` on the map.\nEleven stations are within two stops of Central. Inverting that selection picks out the\nother nine, out at the ends of the lines:\n\n::: {#a4745317 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro()\n(\n    metro\n    .select_nodes_in_neighborhood(\"Central\", k=2)\n    .invert_node_selection()\n)\n\nlabel = metro.get_label_from_id\nsorted(label(n) for n in metro.get_selected_node_ids())\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n['Airport',\n 'Business Park',\n 'Docks',\n 'Garden',\n 'Hillcrest',\n 'Lakeside',\n 'Northpark',\n 'Shipyard',\n 'Westgate']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#4532fb7b .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", highlight=\"selection\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--